# Versions, upgrades and the library pin

`docs/RUNBOOKS.md` § Upgrades is canonical. This page is the two flows an agent
runs most.

## Bumping a version pin

Every chart, image and binary version is single-sourced in
`ansible/inventories/prod/group_vars/all.yml`. Manifests spell them as
`${<name>_version}` and Flux substitutes at reconcile time.

1. `task maintenance:check-versions` lists what is behind.
2. Edit the pin in `all.yml`. Never hand-edit the generated ConfigMap.
3. `task flux:sync-versions`, then commit both files in one commit. The drift
   gate inside `task lint` fails if they disagree.
4. `task flux:lint` if the chart's values changed.
5. Read the release notes for a CRD change. A chart that manages its own CRDs can
   DELETE them on an upgrade or a downgrade, taking every object of that kind
   with it.

Fold every available bump into a revision you are already making rather than
opening a revision just for bumps, and read the pipeline's version-check output
rather than a local run, whose cache can be stale.

## Bumping the library pin

The roles, CI job templates, Terraform modules and vendored gates all come from
weisssrv-lib at `{{ lib_ref }}`. A behaviour change is a library merge request and
a release tag, then a pin bump here.

1. The change lands in the library and a release tag is cut.
2. Here: bump the collection version in `ansible/requirements.yml` and the single
   ref variable in `.gitlab-ci.yml`, then run `scripts/check-lib-pins.py --fix`.
   The Terraform module `?ref=` pins are bumped by hand; a missed one is caught
   by the pin-parity test, not by the fixer.
3. `task lib:sync` to refresh the local checkout, re-vendor the byte-identical
   copies, and re-run the gates. A vendored copy edited here is reverted by the
   next re-vendor and reds the byte-identity gate meanwhile.
4. `task ansible:install-collections` — the installer will not refresh an
   already-installed collection without being forced.
5. Land the inventory changes a renamed or emptied variable needs in the SAME
   merge request. Role variables are `| default(...)`-guarded, so a missed rename
   does not fail: it silently takes the role default.
6. Prove pipeline parity before merging. The library serves several consumers, so
   a changed input default changes this pipeline too.

## OS patching and reboots

The maintenance playbooks drain, patch, reboot and uncordon one node at a time,
and the manual CI jobs run them. Do not run two against the same target at once,
and never start a manual deploy while that target's CI deploy job is in flight.
